60,3,1,talk,Servas,,- **Servas**: The candidates are now before us. Let us weigh them against the risks we have just uncovered.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, given the retention data, I am leaning toward the clinic scheduler or the harvest sensor.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"- **Minako**: @Asuka, the clinic scheduler's subscription model is invisible to our credit line, which is a dangerous gap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Minako, that worries me. If we can't borrow against it, how do we fund the staffing they'll need?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, the scheduler faces medical record security reviews, which historically add three quarters before any revenue starts.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: @Minako, the scheduler faces medical record security reviews, which historically add three quarters before any revenue starts.""}]}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Toshio, that timeline is critical. We must ensure our reporting cycle can absorb a three-quarter delay without straining our quarter-end.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Toshio, that delay is unacceptable. I prefer the harvest sensor; its field instruments give us verifiable data and avoid that review bottleneck.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the sensor's hardware triggers outside appraisals at quarter-end, adding six weeks and fees we cannot afford.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Minako"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Minako: @Asuka, the sensor's hardware triggers outside appraisals at quarter-end, adding six weeks and fees we cannot afford.""}]}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Minako, that appraisal cost is painful, but the sensor team needs seasonal field crews, which recruiters can't place quickly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, that staffing delay is exactly the external bottleneck I feared. The sensor's hardware also risks controller shortages, unlike pure software.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Toshio, you are right. The hardware risks compound. We must consider the ledger bridge, which avoids these physical and regulatory traps.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, the ledger bridge is pure software. We cannot verify its figures independently, only trust its own dashboard.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"-Minako: @Asuka, true, but unlike the scheduler, its merchant data might count as security, giving us borrowing capacity.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Minako, that is a relief. But if it is pure software, who fills the rollout roles when they inevitably ask for help?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, rollout roles fill within weeks. The ledger bridge avoids the hardware and regulatory delays that plague the other options.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Toshio, agreed. The ledger bridge balances verifiable data with manageable staffing. I vote for it.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Servas, I cannot vote for what I cannot verify. The ledger bridge's self-reported figures are a blind spot I will not ignore.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, I vote for the ledger bridge. Its merchant data offers the borrowing capacity we desperately need, unlike the other options.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Servas, I vote for the ledger bridge. Fast staffing and no hardware delays make it the safest bet for us.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, I vote for the ledger bridge. It avoids the external delays and hardware risks that have plagued our recent cohorts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
